# O11F-TEARDOWN acceptance (tests/probes/listening-o11ft-acceptance.py), written by the independent acceptance author.
# This is the TARGET: every check passes. On main 6f9c7a3 (2.7.0, load 3-17) these fail, for the brief's crash: I2/I3
# (the shipped window segfaults at interpreter teardown after Ctrl+C with a room playing: 3 of 200 runs), O2/O3 and
# R2/R3 for shown and playing (a probe child that returns with its window open, or raises, segfaults or aborts at
# teardown: 79 of 80 runs), and N3 (no CHANGELOG entry yet). Every other check passes on main. Evidence and
# readings: the O11F-TEARDOWN acceptance phase-1 report.
# Author-set limits, ruled by the coordinator in phase 1: EXIT_S 15 s, the run counts (10 for the reproducing
# probe-child states, 200 for Ctrl+C with a room playing, 20 elsewhere; the cheaper 10 was declined) and READY_S 120 s.
# Entries with @@ declare the measured part of the name; everything else must match exactly.
