# S1 [ORIGINAL, superseded by the line below in phase 2]: generated from the main run made with 120 Ctrl+C runs; with
# the ruled 200 there are 80 more stops (and 80 more entered rooms), so the stop counts are 440 and 280.
# [ORIGINAL] S1 every session service stopped by SIGTERM removed its socket and left a readable session.json (360 stops)
S1 every session service stopped by SIGTERM removed its socket and left a readable session.json (440 stops)
# S2 [ORIGINAL, superseded by the line below in phase 2]: generated from the main run made with 120 Ctrl+C runs; with
# the ruled 200 there are 80 more stops (and 80 more entered rooms), so the stop counts are 440 and 280.
# [ORIGINAL] S2 after a room was entered, the stopped service's session.json names it as the last session (200 stops)
S2 after a room was entered, the stopped service's session.json names it as the last session (280 stops)
N3 the CHANGELOG records the fix under [Unreleased]: users could hit it (Ctrl+C on the shipped window with a room playing crashed on main), so the section names the crash and the quit or exit
N1 negative control: a deliberate SIGSEGV in the window while its room plays is reported as a crash
N2 negative control: a deliberate SIGSEGV in a probe child where it would return is reported as a crash through xvfb-run and dbus-run-session
